    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d602">

                <pb facs="0863" n="731" xml:id="pg731"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5045/391: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-10-12T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 12,
                                1926—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 12—9:35
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>471. My 466, October 9, 4 p.m.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d602-f1"/> Following from
                    American consul general at Canton: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“October 11, 2 p.m. Kuomintang and strike committee issued lengthy
                            statements yesterday declaring boycott ended but reaffirming intention
                            to carry into effect ‘economic struggle’ with renewed vigor against the
                            British and imperialists generally throughout China. A few Chinese came
                            on the Island<anchor n="37" xml:id="d602-f2"/> today but the general
                            public seems very slow to resume pre-strike relations, and it is still
                            too early to judge the situation. There were no disorders.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
